-- title:
--   Universal property of the disjoint-line locus for pairs
-- statement:
--   Fix primes $q,q'$ and rationals $a,b$ such that $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ satisfies `IsIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt`, i.e. $a>0$ or $b>0$ and, for every height-one prime $v$ of the integers of $\mathbb{Q}$, every nonzero element of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ is a unit exactly when $v$ divides $q$ or $q'$; let $\Lambda$ be a maximal order in it (an order containing $1$, closed under multiplication, spanning over $\mathbb{Q}$, finitely generated, and maximal such). Let $N,m$ be naturals, $\mathcal{O}$ a commutative ring in which $m$ is a unit, and let $(M,\pi_M,\mathrm{ptF})$ be a fine moduli scheme over $\mathcal{O}$ for pairs $(E,P)$ consisting of a fake elliptic curve with $\Lambda$-action and level-$N$ structure over a ring $S$ together with a full level-$m$ structure: $\mathrm{ptF}$ is constant on isomorphism classes, compatible with base change, and bijective from isomorphism classes onto $S$-points of $M$ over any $s:\operatorname{Spec} S\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}$. Let $\ell$ be a prime dividing $m$ and $L_0\le\Lambda$ a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule containing $\ell\Lambda$, stable under left multiplication by $\Lambda$, of relative index $\ell^2$ in $\Lambda$. Let $V\subseteq M$ be an open whose $S$-points are exactly those $\mathrm{ptF}(S,s,w)$ for which, over every algebraically closed field $k$ with $sk:S\to k$ and for every $x\in L_0\cap\Lambda$, the point $x\cdot\bigl((m/\ell)\,P_{k}\bigr)$ equals the identity as soon as it factors through the level-$N$ structure of $w$. Let $\pi_T:T\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}$ and let $\mathrm{pt}'$ assign to each ring $S$, each $s$ and each pair $(E,K)$ with $K$ an extra level at $\ell$ a morphism $\operatorname{Spec} S\to T$ over $s$, constant on isomorphism classes of such pairs (`hiso`) and compatible with pullbacks of pairs along ring maps $\varphi$ with $\operatorname{Spec}\varphi$ followed by $s$ equal to $s'$ (`hpb`). Then there is a unique morphism $\Phi:V\to T$ with $\Phi$ followed by $\pi_T$ equal to the open immersion $V\to M$ followed by $\pi_M$, such that for all $S$, $s$, every $w$ with full level $m$, every extra level $K$ at $\ell$ on its curve, and every $x:\operatorname{Spec} S\to V$ whose composite with the immersion is $\mathrm{ptF}(S,s,w)$: if over every algebraically closed field $k$ with $sk:S\to k$ the geometric points factoring through $K$ are exactly the points $y\cdot\bigl((m/\ell)\,P_{k}\bigr)$ with $y\in L_0\cap\Lambda$, then $\mathrm{pt}'(S,s,(w_1,K))$ equals $x$ followed by $\Phi$.
--
--   This is the representability statement used to produce morphisms out of the open locus of the fine moduli scheme where the $L_0$-line generated by the full level-$m$ point meets the level-$N$ structure trivially: any rule on pairs (fake elliptic curve, extra level at $\ell$) that is isomorphism-invariant and compatible with base change factors uniquely through that locus. It is the analogue for pairs of the universal property of the fine moduli scheme itself, and is invoked in the construction of a coarse moduli scheme for the $\ell$-level quotient in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the development.
